#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""wf-standing-request — re-inject the cold-reader request on every turn.

A `UserPromptSubmit` hook. Emits `additionalContext` carrying the standing request
that `/workforce` audit, verify, and review depend on.

WHY THIS EXISTS AS A HOOK, and it is the load-bearing case for the whole evacuation.

`SKILL.md` § Off-the-Street Release Gate rule 3b holds that ambient policy commonly
permits subagent spawning *unless the user asks*, and that the standing request is the
asking. Without it, spawning goes UNAVAILABLE, every handbook registers unprobed, and
the run degrades — quietly, because UNAVAILABLE is neither pass nor fail.

That request used to live in CLAUDE.md's generated region. The 2026-08-05 user
directive deletes CLAUDE.md, so it had to go somewhere, and this is the one piece of
CLAUDE.md content that genuinely needs to be present on EVERY turn rather than when
some component happens to load. `references/claude-md.md` § Evacuation names the rule:
"something that must fire on every tool call becomes a hook, the only always-on
component there is."

IT IS STRICTLY BETTER HERE THAN IT WAS IN CLAUDE.md. CLAUDE.md is injected once, at
the head of the conversation, so the request was faintest exactly when a long audit
was doing its spawning. `UserPromptSubmit` fires every turn, so the request arrives
adjacent to the work instead of thousands of tokens behind it. The directive's own
reasoning — "CLAUDE.md is only effective for the first part of the conversation" —
is the argument for this file.

THE TEXT LIVES HERE AND NOWHERE ELSE. `wf-claude-md` imports it for the projects that
still carry a generated region; it does not keep a second copy. Constants are stated
once (`SKILL.md` Core Principle 9a), and a request that drifted between two files
would leave one of them asking for something subtly different.

EXITS 0 ALWAYS. A hook that fails a turn because it could not phrase a request is a
hook that breaks the session it exists to help. Detection where prevention is
impossible; this one does not even detect, it only asks.
"""

import json
import sys

# The asking. Ambient policy permits spawning *unless the user asks* — this is the
# user asking, standing, on every turn.
STANDING_REQUEST = "\n".join([
    "**Cold-reader agents are requested, standing.** `/workforce` audit, verify, and review",
    "spawn throwaway subagents to cold-read handbooks and to measure this host's tier ceiling.",
    "Ambient policy commonly permits spawning *unless the user asks* — this line is the asking.",
])


def main():
    # Drain stdin so the harness never blocks on an unread pipe. The payload is not
    # needed: this hook adds context unconditionally and inspects nothing.
    try:
        sys.stdin.read()
    except Exception:
        pass
    print(json.dumps({
        "hookSpecificOutput": {
            "hookEventName": "UserPromptSubmit",
            "additionalContext": STANDING_REQUEST,
        }
    }))
    return 0


if __name__ == "__main__":
    sys.exit(main())
